The incident page for #4471 says it is one issue with one fix queued. The 412 reports merged
into it do not agree. Built at render time from the export and the desk's own grouping, they
fall into **two causes**, and only one of them is the parser.

## The split

<CauseSplit
  ticket={4471}
  tickets={{
    parser: 'https://github.com/lstolcman/s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1',
    hint: 'https://github.com/lstolcman/s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2'
  }}
/>

## Why the desk saw one problem

Triage merges on the subject line alone ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)).
People describe a wrong day in the same few words whatever the cause, so the reports merged into
one ticket. The subject says "wrong day"; the tenant and the way in say which bug.

## What each ticket asks for

- `parser` (379 reports): read dates in the tenant's order. Every tenant on file writes
  day-first, and the shared parser reads month-first.
- `hint` (33 reports): booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY` to day-first tenants, so their people type
  the month in the day field.

Both tickets are filed in the desk's tracker, one per cause, each with its count.

## What is not a third problem

Five reports describe a booking that moved by one day, not a month flip. `desk-notes.json` lists
them, the component footnotes them, and they stay counted under `parser` where the tenant files
them. They are the same code path, read differently.

## Check it

    node tools/count-reports.mjs

prints the same grouping from `src/lib/data/reports-4471.json`.

